ergon-io warning: T1 warn: CPU 9 (loop) is not nohz_full: this kernel has no NO_HZ_FULL (no /sys/devices/system/cpu/nohz_full), so its scheduler tick keeps firing, CONFIG_HZ times a second. On AWS c7i a gap-spinner's CPU took 1,002 local-timer interrupts a second without nohz_full and 0 with it, and had 60,120 and 60,130 gaps over 5 µs a minute on the stock boot, 60,063 and 60,046 with isolcpus alone, 50 and 21 with nohz_full too (longest gap 147/150, 52/30 and 134/30 µs; two runs, one 120 s sample per boot). Fix: use a kernel built with CONFIG_NO_HZ_FULL=y and boot with `isolcpus=nohz,domain,managed_irq,9 nohz_full=9 rcu_nocbs=9 irqaffinity=0-8` (evidence: git show 128747b9^:io/benches/results/flags-aws-20261014T163114Z/tables-local.md (noise table, lines 27-30; interrupts table, lines 332-335) and 128747b9^:io/benches/results/flags-aws-20261015T045527Z/tables-local.md (lines 146-149, 403-406): AWS c7i, one 120 s gap-spinner sample per boot profile; Linux Documentation/timers/no_hz.rst and admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt (isolcpus, nohz_full, rcu_nocbs, irqaffinity)) (ERGON_HOST_CHECKS=off silences host-check warnings)
